tell your story  if you only have one shot to make an  impression on a new potential client the  best thing you can do is not pitch them  but tell your story because it's  authentic because they'll listen to it  because it's real  and because it's something that nobody  else is doing  i got a question today from uh  one of my readers  rajiv hope i pronounce that properly  who's a life insurance agent and he has  a great opportunity ahead of him a  company came to him and basically he won  a chance to do a 30-second video  that they're going to shoot and produce  for him and he wrote in to say what  should i talk about in this video my  best advice for you for that 30 second  clip your one chance to make an  impression and have a professional image  out there is to tell your story  don't pitch some insurance product don't  go on about the benefits of using life  insurance you have one chance to make a  lasting impression and it's gonna come  from telling your story  when you tell your story people relate  to you more they like you they know you  they trust you they want to learn more  about you they feel like this is  somebody  who i can relate to  and when people can relate to you  they're more likely to buy whatever  product or service it is that you're  selling don't lead  with the product lead with yourself  especially when you're in a hugely  competitive industry listening life  insurance there's nothing that you're  selling that i can't get from somebody  else that's the nature of the beast  you're in a heavily commoditized  business and the best way to stand out  the only way you're gonna stand out is  throwing more of yourself into your  business  why did you start this company what are  you trying to accomplish  why do you love this what excites you  about this company let that shine  through  if you're excited and you're passionate  and you're honest and you're real  people will be drawn to you  and they'll want to work with you  if i was going to do something if i had  a quick pitch  i might do something like this  hi i'm evan carmichael i believe in  entrepreneurs  i had my first company when i was 19  years old i was all excited to start  this business up and soon discovered it  was way harder than i thought it was  going to be  and i thought about shutting down almost  every day i was making 300 a month and  couldn't survive and had to tell my  friends that i couldn't go out to dinner  with them  mostly because i couldn't afford it  i made it through i was one of the lucky  ones  eighty percent of businesses failed but  i made it through and now i teach  entrepreneurs how to do it  i'd love to help you if you want to do  something different in this world if you  want to start a business not just  because you're trying to make a lot of  money but because you see a different  future and you want to have an impact  then i want to help you  and i look forward to hearing from you  something like that okay that was just  spur of the moment i don't know if that  was 30 seconds however long it was but  with some practice  you can make it amazing  tap into your story  why you started this what you hope to  accomplish make it real make it  authentic and people will be drawn to  you  now this is really hard for anybody  who's first doing video it's super super  hard  i remember my first videos were terrible  you go back on my youtube channel you'll  see how bad they were  it's really nerve-wracking and the best  advice i can give you is really prepare  in advance so don't memorize a script  because that never works  you'll be looking into the camera like  this  and then trying to look off to the side  or trying to read something that's just  above the camera it makes you look like  you're not actually reading  you could tell  practice your pitch have something  written down practice it over and over  and over and over again but when a time  comes time to actually delivering it get  rid of the actual script  stop trying to memorize  go with what feels right  and try to ignore the people who are in  the room filming you because it is  nerve-wracking just talking into a  camera  and try to imagine your customer your  potential customer in front of you and  the message that you want to get out to  them you want to touch them in this 30  second opportunity  so practice practice practice  hope you guys enjoyed this video if you  do like it please give it a thumbs up  below it always makes me want to do more  for you and i want to hear what you have  to think please leave a comment below if  you agreed with my opinion here or if  you have a question for your company  leave it below and i'll make a video  response thank you so much and i'll see  you soon

